{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Bee Sentinel Auto-Process",
  "description": "Best-effort automatic processing: fires when the sync writes a new sentinel to .kiro/bee-inbox/. Processes the capture per the bee-processing steering and deletes the sentinel when done. Kiro agent hooks only fire while the workspace is open and can miss background writes — if sentinels pile up, run the 'Process Bee Inbox (manual)' hook, which is the reliable fallback.",
  "version": "3",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileCreated",
    "patterns": [
      ".kiro/bee-inbox/*.sentinel.md"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A new Bee sentinel appeared in `.kiro/bee-inbox/`. Process any pending sentinels now, following the SAME close-the-loop procedure as the manual 'Process Bee Inbox' hook (process all pending, not just the one that triggered — the sync may have written several).\n\n1. **Enumerate** every `*.sentinel.md` in `.kiro/bee-inbox/` (ignore `.gitkeep`, `_staging/`, `_output/`).\n2. **Read** each sentinel's frontmatter for `conversation_id` and `raw_path`.\n3. **Idempotency guard:** if the vault already has an output whose frontmatter `bee_conversation_id` matches, SKIP processing but still delete the stale sentinel in step 6.\n4. **Completeness (backstop):** read the raw file (`Get-Content -Raw`, it's outside the workspace). Process ONLY if `state: COMPLETED` AND `end_time` is a real timestamp (not `n/a`). If `state: CAPTURING` or `end_time: n/a`, leave the sentinel and note it will re-fire when complete. If a COMPLETED capture still looks sparse (only a Short Summary), it may still be enriching — skip and let the next pass pick it up.\n5. **Process** per the `bee-processing` steering in auto-process mode (no proposing): apply the redaction policy, and write the three outputs — tasks (`00 Inbox/Bee/`), meeting notes (`05 Reference/[EMPLOYER]/Meeting Notes/` or `05 Reference/Meeting Notes/`), and selective People notes. Every output MUST carry `bee_conversation_id: <id>` in frontmatter. People notes only for high-signal people; append-mode for existing notes; update [YOUR_NAME].md Observed Patterns with genuinely new patterns.\n6. **Close the loop:** DELETE each sentinel after its outputs are written (or after confirming it's a duplicate/already-processed). Partial captures keep their sentinel.\n7. **Summarize** in one or two sentences: what was written and where, plus how many were skipped or left pending. Do not recap meeting contents."
  }
}
